  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Branch quick-intent: what changes",
      "items": [
        "The UI offers five quick-action buttons for the most common questions",
        "AIP_QUICK_ACTIONS=intent: a button with its own text skips the classifier (account intent); the agent still answers with the model and the bank tools",
        "A button is trusted only with its exact text; anything else is classified as usual",
        "Trace reports group turns by routing (model / intent) and quick action"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Request path",
      "items": [
        "The API serves the web UI and streams each agent run as Server-Sent Events",
        "Admission before a run: 20 requests/min per user (per replica) and a daily token quota read from usage_events",
        "nginx adds 30 r/m per client IP on /v1/ and 6 r/m on sign-in; port 80 only redirects to HTTPS",
        "/v1/admin/ (usage, handoffs) answers only requests from the host machine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Agent graph",
      "items": [
        "A quick-action button with its own text gives the intent (account) and skips the classifier; other messages go to the LLM classifier",
        "human → open handoff: the bot stays quiet until the operator closes it",
        "attack → fixed reply, no agent, no tools",
        "account → the first model call must use a bank tool; general and out-of-scope get no tools",
        "Model and tools loop up to 8 iterations; irreversible tools become pending actions that wait for approval",
        "Insistence without resolution offers a human advisor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Sign-in and sessions",
      "items": [
        "Passwords stored as Argon2id hashes; the browser holds an opaque token in an HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict cookie and the database only its SHA-256",
        "5 failed sign-ins lock an account for 15 min; sessions end after 30 min idle or 8 h",
        "One answer for every failure, so usernames cannot be probed",
        "Other modes: OIDC bearer JWT verified against the issuer's JWKS; dev header mode is refused in production"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Bank data isolation",
      "items": [
        "The app connects as bank_reader in read-only transactions with a 5 s statement timeout",
        "Each query first sets app.subject to the signed-in user; Row-Level Security then shows only that customer's rows",
        "The customer comes from the session: the model cannot pass a customer ID or account number",
        "scripts/users.py names accounts after the email's first part and writes the only plain-text passwords to credentials/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Tracing privacy",
      "items": [
        "Off unless enabled; every payload passes the Masker before it leaves the process",
        "Values returned by bank tools stay masked for the rest of the run and in later turns",
        "Trace user is the bank customer ID, else a keyed hash; the username is never sent",
        "The gateway adds one generation per model attempt with tokens and cost",
        "Scores per trace: intent, outcome, prompt_injection"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Model calls and operations",
      "items": [
        "Providers are tried in AIP_PROVIDERS order; a conversation sticks to the provider that served it",
        "Up to 3 attempts per provider with backoff, then failover; SDK retries are disabled",
        "Ollama (local model, dev default) and the Bedrock and Vertex clients go through the same gateway when AIP_PROVIDERS lists them",
        "Without AIP_DATABASE_URL the stores are in-memory; password mode requires the database in production",
        "Prometheus metrics on the internal port 9090; Alembic migrations run as the migrate service"
      ]
    }
  ]
